  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The narrator is a construction with a position, a knowledge limit and an attitude. Equating narrator with author is the commonest error in prose questions.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    First person confines the reader to one account, which is exactly why it can produce suspicion and intimacy.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    More than one mind entered is omniscience. Limited enters one mind; objective enters none.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    No minds at all: the reader must infer everything from what could be filmed. That restraint is the technique.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The third person and past tense carry an attitude that belongs to the character, without a “she thought” to mark it.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Unreliability is a gap between the account and what the reader can infer — from contradiction, correction or self-interest.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The reader lives inside one version and can doubt it, which is the form's characteristic pleasure.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The narrator can enter anywhere, and can therefore judge and compare what the characters cannot.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Flat characters are built on one trait; round characters can contradict themselves credibly.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Change is the dynamic axis. Roundness is a separate question about complexity, and the paper often offers one for the other.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The foil works by contrast, so its function is relational rather than structural.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A report tells you about the reporter as well as the subject, which is why it is evidence twice over.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    When comment contradicts what has been shown, the narrator is being ironic and the reader must judge between them.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Showing dramatises and telling summarises. Neither is automatically superior; the choice is the technique.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Place, time and social world constrain what characters can do, and that constraint is what setting contributes to theme.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Atmosphere is emotional climate, produced by description and diction, and distinct from the physical place.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    In medias res means into the middle of things; the past arrives later as explanation.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The outer telling situation frames the inner tale, and the frame colours how the tale is read.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Episodes give range and variety but weaken causal tension, which is the trade-off the paper tests.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The return to the opening measures change — or its absence — against a world that has stayed the same.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Opening, withholding and closing are decisions, and each one shapes what the reader carries forward.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The motif accumulates meaning across appearances; a symbol can be read once and fixed.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The bildungsroman makes the self its subject; the picaresque makes the rogue's episodes its subject.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Letters replace the narrator, and the gaps between them become part of the meaning.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Allegory sustains a second level of meaning across the whole work; a symbol may be local and suggestive.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The moral is delivered rather than implied, which separates fable from the short story.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The fantastic is narrated in the same tone as the everyday, and nobody in the book finds it remarkable.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The contract with the reader differs, but the technique is the novel's technique, so the same analysis applies.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Word choice. Sentence length is syntax, point of view is position and chapter arrangement is structure.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Reading time imitates event time, and the absence of connectives removes explanation, which is what shock feels like.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Unspecified sensory language could describe any passage, so it distinguishes nothing about this one.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Summary is a tool of pace: it carries the years the reader does not need to experience minute by minute.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Some narrators address a “you” inside the text, and that addressee shapes what can be said and how.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Central first person is the hero telling his own story; peripheral first person is a witness telling someone else's.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Standing at the edge of the action, he reports what he can see, and the hero keeps an unknowable interior.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The last sentence is a decision about what the reader holds, and a question is the strongest thing to hold.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The dumb show is a dramatic device. The other three are prose forms.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Titles direct attention — to an object, a phrase or a character — and questions about them are questions about emphasis.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Adjectives are diction, and the claim links word choice to attitude, which is the correct shape of a style answer.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Beginning, withholding and reordering are plot decisions, and they are invisible if you only follow the story.
  ]

]

